@OpenAI @Thsottiaux Love my DOT AI buddy, but any chance we could get a little more control over what it accesses in the background?

If I ask it not to read something unless I explicitly request it, that preference should be enforced before any data is accessed. Task-specific permissions, an easy pause button, and a simple activity log showing what was accessed and why would go a long way.

I've got about 5 days of "alerts" of this activity continuing to repeat. At least it's honest!

@elonmusk @bot Just tried Grok Bot for the first time!
It found a highly-rated hair salon near me, checked open slots, and booked the appointment. Felt exactly like a personal concierge.
It even asked if I wanted to use the points I still had on the booking site, and double-checked with me
